# 3. Definitions

## 3.1 PII
**Personally Identifiable Information (PII):** Data that can identify an individual.

## 3.2 SPII
**Sensitive Personally Identifiable Information (SPII):** Highly sensitive personal data requiring stronger protection.

## 3.3 Sender
The user who shares data through CLOAKID.

## 3.4 Receiver
The user who receives and views shared data.

## 3.5 Encryption
The process of converting data into a secure format to prevent unauthorized access.

## 3.6 Decryption
The process of converting encrypted data back into readable form.

## 3.7 HTTPS
**Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure (HTTPS):** A protocol used for secure communication over the internet using encryption through TLS/SSL.

## 3.8 Redaction
The process of hiding sensitive parts of data, such as through blurring or pixelation.

## 3.9 Watermark
A visible mark added to data to indicate ownership and help prevent misuse.

## 3.10 MFA
**Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA):** An authentication approach requiring additional verification beyond basic credentials. CLOAKID requires verified users and describes multi-factor authentication as part of its authentication process.

## 3.11 Access Control
Rules and restrictions that determine how and for how long a receiver can access shared data.

## 3.12 Activity Log
A record of actions performed on shared data, including access, views, requests, and permitted resharing activity.
